  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe propose to use a multi-resolution variational approach that optimizes the step function over a grid of candidate points, combined with a directed evolution technique. The key idea is to represent the step function using a sparse matrix formulation derived from its piecewise constant nature, and then evolve this representation through local extrema. We address local optima by projecting solutions to different grid resolutions and using mutation operators based on the divergence of gradient information. The algorithm combines three novel components:\n1. A transformed coordinate system that aligns with the periodic correlation structure\n2. A quadratic penalty for large gradient variances\n3. A resolution transfer mechanism between grid levels\n\nThe approach differs from the parent since it:\n- Uses grid sparsification to represent correlations more accurately\n- Projects gradient information rather than sequences\n- Includes a layered refinement strategy (coarse-to-fine then fine-to-coarse)\n- Uses divergence-based stopping criteria\n\nMathematical specification:\nThe step function is represented by n samples. We constrained the optimization using:\n- $ \\sum_i h[i] = N/2 $\n- $ 0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1 $\n\nThe objective is minimized by:\n$ \\min \\max_{k} \\| T_{k} h \\| $ where $ T_{k} $ is the Toeplitz operator for shift k.\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Initialization:\n   - Start with initial grid parent if available\n   - Initialize grid with uniform spacing dx=2/n\n   - Compute correlation for all shifts\n\n2. Coarse-to-fine (500s budget):\n   - Downsample to n_coarse (n//2) points\n   - Solve variational problem on coarser grid\n   - Interpolate to full grid\n\n3. Fine-to-coarse evolution (400s budget):\n   - Project gradient directions to fewer points\n   - Iterate penalty function (grad_pen = $\\sum_i|\\partial h[i]|^2$)\n   - Include momentum and divergence-based learning\n   - Compute move decisions using thresholded gradient\n\n4. Refinement (150s budget):\n   - Run synchronous multi-start local search\n   - Project solutions to satisfy constraints\n   - Track top 5 evolution paths\n\nSearch choices:\n- n_grids = [4,8,16,32,64,128] points (coarse to fine)\n- grad_pen_scale = 5.0 (adaptive based on gradient variance)\n- delta_t = 0.95 (momentum parameter)\n- Resampling frequency = 100s (1d evolution, 50s validation)\n\nBudget and robustness:\n- Total time: 1050s\n- Monitor at 60s intervals\n- Check valid overlap at midpoint of epochs\n- If divergence detected, reduce learning rate\n- Keep base solution valid throughout gradient descent\n- Return best valid solution found\n\nValidation and return:\n- Final candidate passed through clipping and integral projection\n- Objective recomputed using the provided evaluator\n- Check gradient diversity before termination\n- Normalize output to [0,1] with exact N/2 integral",
